# An example of a basic measures declaration. 
# As the example illustrates, while it is possible that concepts, types, units and measure have
# different names, it is allowable for their names to be the same since the semantics of CPL
# have been defined so that the use of a name is always unambiguous in terms of whether the
# reference is to a concept, a type, a unit or a measure.

concepts
    Currency = [Values[USD, Euro, Yen]]

types
    Currency = Number(precision=2)
    CurrencyType = Number(precision=2)

units
    CurrencyUnit = Currency
    Currency = Currency
    

measures
    CurrencyMeasure = CurrencyType(unit=CurrencyUnit)
    Currency = Currency(unit=Currency)
